{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nWhile validating documentation-only leaf 717a-ebd1-42f0-4dec at exact commit d12389b8d840dee4c10ddd48e7e1801aad7373ee, the focused interface suite timed out in test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass. The stack was blocked in subprocess.run for git -C <fresh repo> remote get-url origin, called by write_blocking_divergence during import_tickets. This ran concurrently with other bounded local validation. Closed bug bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f explicitly says a recurrence on a fresh store needs a separate investigation; its mature-store foreground-maintenance fix does not explain this fresh-store occurrence.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce under controlled idle and concurrent-load conditions in an isolated worktree.\n- Capture the exact git child argv, duration, process state, and host load at the stall.\n- Distinguish scheduler or I/O starvation, inherited git configuration or hooks, credential-helper behavior, and a fixture or store-path defect with one-variable experiments.\n- Fix the proven failure class and add a deterministic regression oracle without weakening time bounds.\n\n## Testing\n- RED: `pytest tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::<new lowcost regression>` must fail before the fix by showing batched import still calls write_blocking_divergence per buffered event.\n- GREEN targeted: `pytest tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::<new lowcost regression> tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py`.\n- Final verification: `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8` with ambient GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The timeout mechanism is reproduced or falsified with recorded evidence.\n- [ ] Competing hypotheses receive discriminating experiments and verdicts.\n- [ ] Any fix targets the proven class and has RED-before-GREEN regression coverage.\n- [ ] The affected focused interface suite passes reliably under its supported concurrency envelope.\n- [ ] Findings and residual risks are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788906945923379001,"uuid":"19f42e8b-3e9c-42a3-91bd-edaee6b248dd"}